{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg39pHo1gxVdNofpDWZ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`~/basic-memory/ufo` can't be created because it would sit inside the existing `main` project. `main` is empty, so I'll use it as the primary project and seed the schemas there."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":32479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c8a2db0-7e64-4909-9e56-07b3c989741b","uuid":"96099231-0e36-4dc3-aaed-5433fd01828a","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:01:18.832Z","request_id":"req_011Cgg39p2vQcJh6iX47d2FZ"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg39pHo1gxVdNofpDWZ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WjxMPvjBiwbp4RN853FbmJ","name":"mcp__basic-memory__bm_write","input":{"project":"main","directory":"schemas","title":"Coding Session","note_type":"schema","content":"# Coding Session\n\nA **CodingSession** is a resumable engineering checkpoint whose repository\nidentity is structured and queryable. Required Git fields make it possible to\nfind the exact work cursor without parsing prose.\n\nExamples:\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"repository\": \"owner/repo\"})`\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"pull_request_number\": \"123\"})`\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"agent\": \"codex\", \"session_id\": \"<id>\"})`\n\nPull-request fields are optional because valid coding work can precede a pull\nrequest. When a pull request exists, checkpoint writers populate the complete\npull-request field set. Multiple checkpoints from one agent chat share the\n`agent` and `session_id` pair; session IDs alone are not cross-agent identity.\nEach new checkpoint can link to its verified predecessor with\n`continues [[Previous checkpoint title]]`. New writers use the shared fields.\nLegacy agent-specific session fields remain accepted for existing notes; do not\nrewrite old checkpoints or infer missing session IDs.\n","metadata":{"entity":"CodingSession","version":1,"schema":{"summary?":"string, one-paragraph what happened in this coding session","changed_file?(array)":"string, files created, edited, deleted, or inspected","verification?(array)":"string, checks run and their result","decision?(array)":"string, decisions surfaced or created during the session","blocker?(array)":"string, unresolved blockers or failed approaches","next_step?(array)":"string, explicit cursor for the next coding session","produced?(array)":"Entity, notes or artifacts created or updated"},"settings":{"validation":"warn","frontmatter":{"project":"string, the Basic Memory project this session belongs to","started":"string, when the session began or checkpoint was created","repository":"string, stable repository identifier such as owner/name","repo_root":"string, Git repository root for this checkout","cwd":"string, working directory for the session","branch":"string, checked-out Git branch or HEAD when detached","git_sha":"string, exact Git commit at checkpoint time","ended?":"string, when the session was checkpointed","status?(enum, lifecycle of the checkpoint)":["open","resumed","closed"],"pull_request_number?":"string, current pull request number as a queryable identifier","pull_request_title?":"string, current pull request title","pull_request_url?":"string, canonical pull request URL","pull_request_state?(enum, pull request state at checkpoint time)":["open","closed","merged"],"pull_request_base?":"string, pull request base branch","pull_request_head?":"string, pull request head branch","username?":"string, operating-system user that created the checkpoint","hostname?":"string, host that created the checkpoint","session_id?":"string, exact host-provided session identifier (pair with agent)","agent?":"string, agent harness identifier such as tau or claude-code or codex","tau_session_id?":"string, legacy Tau session identifier (read compatibility only)","claude_session_id?":"string, legacy Claude Code session identifier (read compatibility only)","codex_session_id?":"string, legacy Codex session identifier (read compatibility only)","codex_turn_id?":"string, Codex turn identifier","trigger?":"string, compaction trigger or deliberate checkpoint source","model?":"string, active model slug when known","capture?(enum, how this checkpoint was produced)":["extractive","deliberate","summarized"]}}}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":32479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c8a2db0-7e64-4909-9e56-07b3c989741b","uuid":"8b43dcdb-7322-49a5-839f-519e52343c5e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:01:24.587Z","request_id":"req_011Cgg39p2vQcJh6iX47d2FZ","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WjxMPvjBiwbp4RN853FbmJ","display_name":"Write note","server_display_name":"Basic Memory","tool_name":"bm_write"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WjxMPvjBiwbp4RN853FbmJ","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Coding Session.md\\ntitle: Coding Session\\npermalink: main/schemas/coding-session\\nchecksum: 4516eea5805c53d620f88375a781e48efaf73d3ca16c94f4d5729539dcb6752e\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c8a2db0-7e64-4909-9e56-07b3c989741b","uuid":"0786490b-8474-416a-bf38-063a4c3dc2e6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:01:27.294Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Coding Session.md\\ntitle: Coding Session\\npermalink: main/schemas/coding-session\\nchecksum: 4516eea5805c53d620f88375a781e48efaf73d3ca16c94f4d5729539dcb6752e\"}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Basic Memory","version":"4.1.3"},"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"Created schemas/Coding Session.md\ntitle: Coding Session\npermalink: main/schemas/coding-session\nchecksum: 4516eea5805c53d620f88375a781e48efaf73d3ca16c94f4d5729539dcb6752e"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WjxMPvjBiwbp4RN853FbmJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg39pHo1gxVdNofpDWZ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R8XVR31TJhNEai4kAyoxeY","name":"mcp__basic-memory__bm_write","input":{"project":"main","directory":"schemas","title":"Decision","note_type":"schema","content":"# Decision\n\nA **DecisionNote** is a durable record of a real choice — one with alternatives\nand a rationale, not a passing preference. Basic Memory host integrations\nencourage agents to capture these as decisions are made or explicitly requested.\n\nDecisions are found by structured recall:\n`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"decision\", \"status\": \"open\"})`.\n\n## What makes a good DecisionNote\n\n- **decision** — state the choice plainly.\n- **rationale** + **alternative** — why this, and what was rejected. This is the\n  part that saves a future session from relitigating the same ground.\n- **consequence** — what the choice commits the work to.\n- **affects** / **supersedes** — relations that wire the decision into the graph.\n\n## Frontmatter\n\n`type: decision` plus `status` make decisions queryable. Capture decisions\nsparingly — one note per genuine decision, not per opinion. Validation is `warn`,\nnever blocking.\n","metadata":{"entity":"Decision","version":1,"schema":{"decision":"string, the choice that was made","rationale?":"string, why this choice over the alternatives","alternative?(array)":"string, options that were considered and not taken","consequence?(array)":"string, what this decision commits us to","context?":"string, the situation that prompted the decision","affects?(array)":"Entity, work or notes this decision bears on","supersedes?":"Entity, a prior decision this one replaces"},"settings":{"validation":"warn","frontmatter":{"status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision)":["open","accepted","superseded","rejected"],"decided?":"string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)","project?":"string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to"}}}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":32479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c8a2db0-7e64-4909-9e56-07b3c989741b","uuid":"86c2e542-8bc3-49da-bbe9-a980077fa2ff","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:01:27.835Z","request_id":"req_011Cgg39p2vQcJh6iX47d2FZ","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R8XVR31TJhNEai4kAyoxeY","display_name":"Write note","server_display_name":"Basic Memory","tool_name":"bm_write"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R8XVR31TJhNEai4kAyoxeY","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Decision.md\\ntitle: Decision\\npermalink: main/schemas/decision\\nchecksum: bd0b557fa5eb6c83f5db5373d420f221f4861912a4cb7a7c5eabd53d008cbe96\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c8a2db0-7e64-4909-9e56-07b3c989741b","uuid":"c16379e8-d208-4bd5-9165-435c46d3bb12","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:01:28.059Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Decision.md\\ntitle: Decision\\npermalink: main/schemas/decision\\nchecksum: bd0b557fa5eb6c83f5db5373d420f221f4861912a4cb7a7c5eabd53d008cbe96\"}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Basic Memory","version":"4.1.3"},"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"Created schemas/Decision.md\ntitle: Decision\npermalink: main/schemas/decision\nchecksum: bd0b557fa5eb6c83f5db5373d420f221f4861912a4cb7a7c5eabd53d008cbe96"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R8XVR31TJhNEai4kAyoxeY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgg39pHo1gxVdNofpDWZ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018XPyncWc3WVEtENnRxACPY","name":"mcp__basic-memory__bm_write","input":{"project":"main","directory":"schemas","title":"Task","note_type":"schema","content":"# Task\n\nA **Task** is work-in-progress tracked as a note, so it survives context\ncompaction and shows up in the next session's brief. This schema is the same one\nthe framework-agnostic [`memory-tasks`](https://github.com/basicmachines-co/basic-memory/tree/main/skills/memory-tasks)\nskill defines — kept identical here so the plugin and the skill agree on the\nshape. For the full task workflow (creating, updating, completing), use that\nskill.\n\nTasks are found by the SessionStart hook via structured recall:\n`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"task\", \"status\": \"active\"})`.\n\n## Frontmatter vs observations\n\nPut queryable fields (`status`, `priority`, `current_step`) in frontmatter so\n`filters` can find them, and mirror them as `- [status] active`\nobservations so `bm_schema(command=\"validate\")` sees them. `note_type=\"Task\"` is stored as\nlowercase `task` in frontmatter, so search with `note_types=[\"task\"]`.\nValidation is `warn` — advisory, never blocking.\n","metadata":{"entity":"Task","version":1,"schema":{"description":"string, what needs to be done","status?(enum, current state)":["active","blocked","done","abandoned"],"assigned_to?":"string, who is working on this","steps?(array)":"string, ordered steps to complete","current_step?":"integer, which step number we're on (1-indexed)","context?":"string, key context needed to resume after memory loss","started?":"string, when work began","completed?":"string, when work finished","blockers?(array)":"string, what's preventing progress","parent_task?":"Task, parent task if this is a subtask"},"settings":{"validation":"warn"}}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":32479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":443},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c8a2db0-7e64-4909-9e56-07b3c989741b","uuid":"2e28b131-f177-4958-98d6-5fa76cb4646d","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:01:30.680Z","request_id":"req_011Cgg39p2vQcJh6iX47d2FZ","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018XPyncWc3WVEtENnRxACPY","display_name":"Write note","server_display_name":"Basic Memory","tool_name":"bm_write"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018XPyncWc3WVEtENnRxACPY","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Task.md\\ntitle: Task\\npermalink: main/schemas/task\\nchecksum: c5bfe6150d110d1a8673a0d52b7fbafa73cfa26caa88a62a24861c05b4b9fa7b\\n\\n## Similar existing notes\\nThis note looks similar to notes that already exist. Did you mean to write to one of these?\\n- Decision (`schemas/Decision.md`)\\n- Coding Session (`schemas/Coding Session.md`)\\n\\n| If it is... | Then |\\n|---|---|\\n| The same topic | `bm_edit(identifier='schemas/Decision.md', command='append', content='...', project='main')`, then `bm_delete(identifier='schemas/Task.md', project='main')` |\\n| Related but distinct | Add a relation here, e.g. `- relates_to [[Decision]]` |\\n| Unrelated | Nothing to do |\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c8a2db0-7e64-4909-9e56-07b3c989741b","uuid":"6b4b96f3-cf8c-450c-bb0f-70258d85928a","timestamp":"2026-11-03T13:01:30.925Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"Created schemas/Task.md\\ntitle: Task\\npermalink: main/schemas/task\\nchecksum: c5bfe6150d110d1a8673a0d52b7fbafa73cfa26caa88a62a24861c05b4b9fa7b\\n\\n## Similar existing notes\\nThis note looks similar to notes that already exist. Did you mean to write to one of these?\\n- Decision (`schemas/Decision.md`)\\n- Coding Session (`schemas/Coding Session.md`)\\n\\n| If it is... | Then |\\n|---|---|\\n| The same topic | `bm_edit(identifier='schemas/Decision.md', command='append', content='...', project='main')`, then `bm_delete(identifier='schemas/Task.md', project='main')` |\\n| Related but distinct | Add a relation here, e.g. `- relates_to [[Decision]]` |\\n| Unrelated | Nothing to do |\"}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Basic Memory","version":"4.1.3"},"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"Created schemas/Task.md\ntitle: Task\npermalink: main/schemas/task\nchecksum: c5bfe6150d110d1a8673a0d52b7fbafa73cfa26caa88a62a24861c05b4b9fa7b\n\n## Similar existing notes\nThis note looks similar to notes that already exist. Did you mean to write to one of these?\n- Decision (`schemas/Decision.md`)\n- Coding Session (`schemas/Coding Session.md`)\n\n| If it is... | Then |\n|---|---|\n| The same topic | `bm_edit(identifier='schemas/Decision.md', command='append', content='...', project='main')`, then `bm_delete(identifier='schemas/Task.md', project='main')` |\n| Related but distinct | Add a relation here, e.g. `- relates_to [[Decision]]` |\n| Unrelated | Nothing to do |"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018XPyncWc3WVEtENnRxACPY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
